    """How to compare. Text comparisons (`equals`, `notEquals`, `contains`, `notContains`, `startsWith`, `in`) ignore case and accents ("jose" matches "José"). `notEquals` and `notContains` also match contacts without the value. Date operators (`before`, `after`, `withinLastDays`, `moreThanDaysAgo`) compare as dates and times in UTC: a stored ISO-8601 date is the start of that day, `before` means earlier than the given day and `after` later than it, and a value that is not an ISO-8601 date or date and time never matches. `inNextDays` is a date from today to that many days ahead. `anniversaryInNextDays` (0 = today) and `anniversaryThisMonth` ignore the year, so they suit birthdays, and also read a yearless `--MM-DD`; a 29 February counts on 28 February in other years. Days are UTC days; these three are for attributes and dates, not contact fields."""
    value: NotRequired[str]
    """What to compare with, always as text: `"pro"`, `"3"`, `"true"`. Equality compares the stored value as text, so a stored 5 matches `"5"`. An ISO date for `before` and `after`; a number for `gt`, `gte`, `lt` and `lte`; a whole number of days (1 to 3650) for `withinLastDays`, `moreThanDaysAgo` and `inNextDays`, and 0 to 365 for `anniversaryInNextDays`. Omit for `in`, `exists`, `notExists` and `anniversaryThisMonth`."""
    values: NotRequired[list[str]]
    """For `in` only: up to 100 values, each as text, any of which matches."""


