class EventConditionInputWhereItem(TypedDict, total=False):
    property: Required[str]
    """The event property key."""
    operator: Required[Literal["equals", "notEquals", "gt", "gte", "lt", "lte", "before", "after", "withinLastDays", "moreThanDaysAgo", "inNextDays"]]
    """`notEquals` also matches an event without the property. `equals` and `notEquals` ignore case and accents in text. The date operators read the property as a date, as attribute conditions do: UTC days, an ISO-8601 date is the start of that day, and a property that is missing or not an ISO-8601 date or date and time never matches. They read the property's own date; `withinDays` limits when the event happened. Membership moves with the calendar: a contact enters when the date comes into range, with no new event, and a journey triggered by entering the segment then starts for them."""
    value: Required[str]
    """What to compare with, as text: as for the other operators, an ISO date for `before` and `after`, and a whole number of days, `"1"` to `"3650"`, for `withinLastDays`, `moreThanDaysAgo` and `inNextDays`."""


